        "# ============================================================\n",
        "#  DNN CONTROL — same network, NO class weighting\n",
        "#\n",
        "#  Answers the obvious reviewer question: \"was the neural network handicapped\n",
        "#  by your loss weighting?\" The main dnn_shap.py run uses inverse-frequency\n",
        "#  class weights, which on CICIDS2017 reach 184x for the rarest class and push\n",
        "#  the network hard toward recall (macro-P 0.5849, macro-R 0.9809). This cell\n",
        "#  trains the identical architecture with a flat loss and reports detection\n",
        "#  quality, so both rows can go in the table.\n",
        "#\n",
        "#  Explanation cost is NOT re-measured: DeepSHAP's cost depends on the network\n",
        "#  architecture and the background set, not on the loss weights, so the 33 ms\n",
        "#  figure already measured applies to this model too.\n",
        "#\n",
        "#  SAFE TO RUN AFTER dnn_shap.py: it writes to model_unw / scaler_unw and does\n",
        "#  NOT touch `model`, `scaler` or DNN_READY, so resource_benchmark.py keeps\n",
        "#  measuring the weighted network it already measured.\n",
        "#\n",
